    "blurb": "Run quantum circuits in BPMN",
    "overview": "Camunda outbound connector for Amazon Braket. Submit and poll quantum computing jobs from BPMN workflows using OpenQASM circuits. Supports real quantum hardware, simulators, blocking and polling execution, and higher-level quantum algorithms via a Python sidecar.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Integrate quantum computing into your BPMN processes",
    "splashDescription": "The Amazon Braket connector integrates quantum computing into your Camunda processes. Submit quantum circuits written in OpenQASM or as raw JSON parameters directly to Amazon Braket backends, including real quantum hardware and simulators. The connector supports both blocking and non-blocking (polling) execution patterns to handle the unpredictable queue times of real quantum hardware. For higher-level algorithms such as Grover's search or QAOA, an optional Python sidecar generates circuits from classical inputs and interprets measurement results, enabling full variational quantum algorithms with classical optimization loops inside a BPMN process.",
    "imageUrl": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/822036/overview/img3548926509594726309.png?15d11951e891564c6eafea101befad33",
